            <ArticleTitle>Successful laparoscopic exploration and screw extraction for intractable pain after anterior iliosacral arthrodesis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e83-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/BOT.0b013e3181c1d518</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on the case of a patient suffering from L5 radicular pain after previous anterior sacroiliac arthrodesis using 2, 4-hole plates. Technical investigations indicated loosening and migration of a screw from the upper sacroiliac plate, irritating the L5 nerve root. The problem was managed by removal of the screw using an anterior transperitoneal laparoscopic approach.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
